From: vLLM Fedora packaging
Subject: [PATCH] Degrade @torch.compile to eager when unsupported

FP4_E2M1_DATA.cast_to_fp4 is decorated with @torch.compile, which runs at
import time. On some interpreters torch.compile raises unconditionally
(RuntimeError: "torch.compile is not supported on Python 3.15+" with the torch
build shipped in Fedora), which makes the whole compressed_tensors package
unimportable. The helper is numerically correct when run eagerly, so fall back
to the uncompiled function instead of failing at import.

--- a/src/compressed_tensors/quantization/quant_args.py
+++ b/src/compressed_tensors/quantization/quant_args.py
@@ -18,6 +18,19 @@
 )


+def _safe_compile(fn):
+    """Apply torch.compile, falling back to the eager function if unsupported.
+
+    torch.compile raises on some interpreters (RuntimeError on Python 3.15+).
+    The decorated helpers are correct when run eagerly, so degrade to the
+    uncompiled function instead of failing at import time.
+    """
+    try:
+        return torch.compile(fn)
+    except Exception:
+        return fn
+
+
 __all__ = [
     "FP8_E4M3_DATA",
     "FP4_E2M1_DATA",
@@ -53,7 +66,7 @@
     min = -6.0

     @staticmethod
-    @torch.compile
+    @_safe_compile
     def cast_to_fp4(x):
         sign = torch.sign(x)
         x = torch.abs(x)
